00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:40.220
Mayhem on Kamogawa Beach

00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:40.260
<i>Lympha, respond!</i>

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:41.720
<i>Laffinty!</i>

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:45.560
Lan...

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:46.810
<i>Lympha...</i>

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:48.810
<i>Please respond! Lympha...</i>

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:50.310
<i>Lympha!</i>

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:53.980
<i>Lan...</i>

00:02:55.770 --> 00:02:56.940
<i>Lan!</i>

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:14.500
That voice just now...

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:16.380
Madoka!

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:18.630
<i>Aura is approaching the battle zone!</i>

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:20.550
Madoka?!

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:22.510
You two...

00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:23.800
... stop fighting...

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:26.760
... right—

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:35.480
She went right past them.

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:36.230
Huh?

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:41.030
What?

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:45.450
<i>Lympha and Ignis have resumed battle!</i>

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:46.450
Wait...

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:50.080
<i>Hey, what're you doing?!</i>

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:51.250
I have no idea!

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:54.330
Hey, Midori! Snap out of it!

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:56.840
<i>The three of us are finally together again, so why...?</i>

00:03:57.460 --> 00:04:01.010
<i>I was hoping we could get together like we did before.</i>

00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:02.260
What?

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:03.590
What was that?

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:08.560
<i>Why do I have to</i> <i>fight you, Muginami?!</i>

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:10.810
<i>I really... love you, Lan!</i>

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:12.850
Are these their thoughts?

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:15.770
<i>Why won't you understand?!</i>

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:21.900
Stay away from Madoka!

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:22.990
<i>I should be the one saying that!</i>

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:25.200
Your people tried to destroy De Metrio!

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:27.070
Do you plan on being a puppet for your brother forever?!

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:29.280
Look who's talking!

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:31.790
<i>I don't know who started all this, but...</i>

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:34.080
Madoka?

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:35.500
<i>I said...</i>

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:36.790
Stop fighting!

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:54.020
What is wrong with you two?!

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:58.230
You're crazy! Why must you two fight?!

00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:03.110
Say something!

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:04.860
What?

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:07.160
It's the Le Garite Occupation Forces.

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:15.580
Switch to an open channel.

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:19.000
But then Ignis will be able to overhear the transmission.

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:20.250
That's fine...

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:21.500
Kyouno!

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:24.840
<i>A Le Garite platoon is closing in on your position.</i>

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:27.680
<i>They plan to shoot down the enemy unit, Ignis.</i>

00:05:29.050 --> 00:05:31.140
Reinforcements are sure to follow.

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:33.060
Back away so that you do not get mixed up in this.

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:36.600
Huh? What do you mean shoot down Muginami?!

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:38.020
<i>Did you get that?</i>

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:42.190
Thank you...

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:48.700
Muginami?!

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:49.740
Lan, let's go!

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:52.740
<i>I'm sorry, Madoka.</i>

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:54.200
Lan?!

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:56.540
I'm sorry.

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:02.380
"Sorry"?

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:04.340
Hey wait, Lan!

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:07.470
Why are you two...?

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:09.300
I don't get it.

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:10.720
Huh?

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:15.020
Hey... Hey, hey!

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:16.390
Midori?!

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:25.610
<i>I keep telling you that I can't authorize that.</i>

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:27.650
Please let me go search for them!

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:32.780
<i>That's what you get for trying to swim after them.</i>

00:06:33.410 --> 00:06:36.410
<i>We are on the lookout for Lympha and Ignis.</i>

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:39.620
<i>Even if you were to go look for those two with Aura,</i>

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:41.460
<i>you don't have any leads to begin with.</i>

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:47.090
Besides, their fight is part of a galactic dispute between two planets.

00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:51.090
Earth needn't interfere.

00:06:51.090 --> 00:06:54.140
<i>Both of them were acting strange.</i>

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:58.180
Lan and Muginami seemed like they were acting against their will.

00:06:58.180 --> 00:07:01.520
I mean, why are they even fighting in the first place?

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:03.690
<i>Girl, do you understand the words that are coming out of my mouth?</i>

00:07:04.230 --> 00:07:07.940
They finally came back to Kamogawa. So why?

00:07:09.190 --> 00:07:10.400
<i>I guess not...</i>

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:12.860
<i>Wh-What is it this time?!</i>

00:07:14.570 --> 00:07:15.830
That's it.

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:18.750
It's Kamogawa.

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:21.420
That's gotta be it!

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:22.460
Thank you!

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:25.340
Hey, Kyouno? Kyouno?!

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:27.130
She already left.

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:28.090
What?

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:32.720
Lan!

00:07:35.260 --> 00:07:36.260
Muginami!

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:38.720
Huh?

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:40.100
They're not back.

00:07:40.980 --> 00:07:42.640
Oh, welcome home.

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:43.730
They're back!

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:45.980
Man, I'm starving.

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:48.020
Another busy day, wasn't it?

00:07:48.940 --> 00:07:50.650
Hey, what the hell?

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:52.570
Are they back?!

00:07:52.570 --> 00:07:54.740
Oh, hey... Welcome back.

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:56.280
Where are Lan and Muginami?!

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:57.330
Huh?

00:07:57.330 --> 00:08:00.000
Are those two coming back here?

00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:04.920
That's odd... It wasn't Kamogawa then?

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:08.380
I was positive they'd be here.

00:08:08.380 --> 00:08:10.760
Maybe they went home.

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:13.380
I guess so, since they're not here.

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:19.970
Hey, do you guys know where they live?

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:22.980
Do you know?

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:24.390
Do you know?

00:08:24.390 --> 00:08:25.730
I don't know!

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:33.570
I understand Laffinty and Muginami went at it.

00:08:36.360 --> 00:08:40.620
I'm sure this is the motive.

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:43.710
You mean the Thousand Year Polyhedron problem?

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:47.920
The astral phenomenon that will cause the orbits of Le Garite and De Metrio to collide

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:51.840
and result in the destruction of both planets.

00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:54.220
But I was under the impression

00:08:54.220 --> 00:08:58.800
that a plan of action would be discussed at the upcoming intergalactic conference?

00:09:00.310 --> 00:09:04.890
<i>Do you plan on being a puppet for your brother forever?!</i>

00:09:04.890 --> 00:09:07.100
<i>Look who's talking!</i>

00:09:07.690 --> 00:09:14.610
Judging from this recording, Laffinty was trying to get Madoka to pilot Aura under her brother's orders.

00:09:14.610 --> 00:09:20.370
By all accounts, he is willing to destroy De Metrio in order to correct the orbit.

00:09:20.370 --> 00:09:23.040
They believe that Aura has the power to destroy a planet?

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:27.330
According to what Izo and others have said, it's possible.

00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:29.880
Apparently, the princess of De Metrio

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:35.260
destroyed a natural satellite named Militia Zodia during a Vox Core experiment.

00:09:35.260 --> 00:09:36.880
What is a Vox Core?

00:09:37.550 --> 00:09:39.970
It's the prototype of the Vox cockpit.

00:09:40.390 --> 00:09:46.230
In any case, Dizelmine is planning something outside the intergalactic conference

00:09:46.230 --> 00:09:48.730
and intends to make use of Madoka and Aura.

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:51.610
Depending on her actions...

00:09:52.730 --> 00:09:54.780
a full-blown stellar war may very well break out.

00:09:57.240 --> 00:10:00.950
It's no use. I can't detect Ignis' signal.

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:05.870
She's always been good at hiding, that Muginami.

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:08.830
<i>Is this it?</i>

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:10.880
<i>Are we connected to them?</i>

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:13.880
<i>Yeah, as long as they haven't changed their identification signal.</i>

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:18.220
State your ship's affiliation and I.D. number.

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:20.760
This ship belongs to the De Metrio Army.

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:22.140
Hold it, Grania...

00:10:25.310 --> 00:10:27.270
<i>Oh, hello?</i>

00:10:27.270 --> 00:10:30.650
<i>Uh... This is Kyouno Madoka, from Kamogawa.</i>

00:10:41.070 --> 00:10:43.240
Repairs will be expedited and should take about one week.

00:10:44.490 --> 00:10:47.500
We should be done by the time the intergalactic conference starts.

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:48.910
Thank you.

00:10:48.910 --> 00:10:52.420
Are you relieved to see that Aura is operational again?

00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:54.880
Just more hijinks waiting to happen.

00:10:55.750 --> 00:10:57.510
Say, Cap...

00:10:57.510 --> 00:10:58.300
What is it?

00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:00.090
Look...

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:05.100
Hey, Giuvi...

00:11:05.100 --> 00:11:06.890
Is Muginami over there?

00:11:06.890 --> 00:11:08.930
I saw her this afternoon,

00:11:08.930 --> 00:11:12.440
<i>but then she left and now I can't find her anymore.</i>

00:11:12.440 --> 00:11:14.190
"Giuvi"?!

00:11:14.190 --> 00:11:15.520
Who do you think you're talking to?!

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:18.400
<i>Kyouno! What the hell are you doing?!</i>

00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:19.990
<i>Oh, Mr. Tadokoro...</i>

00:11:19.990 --> 00:11:21.110
<i>I'm on the phone.</i>

00:11:21.110 --> 00:11:22.740
<i>That's not what I meant!</i>

00:11:22.740 --> 00:11:23.320
<i>Uehara!</i>

00:11:23.320 --> 00:11:25.240
<i>Intercept her call from the bridge and terminate it!</i>

00:11:25.240 --> 00:11:26.530
<i>W-Wait!</i>

00:11:29.620 --> 00:11:31.210
The nerve these fools have!

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:34.330
You moron!

00:11:34.790 --> 00:11:37.130
Didn't I <i>just</i> order you not to act recklessly?!

00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:40.090
At this point, De Metrio is a hostile force!

00:11:40.090 --> 00:11:43.590
Did you really think you could contact them without clearing it first with the Le Garite Occupation Forces?!

00:11:44.180 --> 00:11:46.720
Why do we have to be here too?

00:11:46.720 --> 00:11:47.640
And you guys...!

00:11:48.220 --> 00:11:51.390
You work for the Chairman, so you have no excuse for not knowing the situation.

00:11:51.390 --> 00:11:52.940
But we do.

00:11:52.940 --> 00:11:55.980
We've been out of the loop for six months.

00:11:55.980 --> 00:11:57.610
Longer than that.

00:11:57.610 --> 00:12:00.400
Aren't you worried about those two, Mr. Tadokoro?

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:04.280
Listen, whether or not I worry about them is not the issue here.

00:12:04.280 --> 00:12:06.320
What is it then?

00:12:06.320 --> 00:12:07.200
Stop!

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:12.330
In any case, those two did not return to their brothers.

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:15.830
If they had left this planet, our surveillance satellites would have caught it.

00:12:15.830 --> 00:12:17.540
Then where are they?

00:12:17.540 --> 00:12:19.090
They haven't left Earth.

00:12:19.670 --> 00:12:22.130
They're still on Earth?

00:12:23.930 --> 00:12:24.840
Hey, Kyouno!

00:12:26.930 --> 00:12:28.970
I'm going back to Kamogawa.

00:12:28.970 --> 00:12:31.810
If they haven't gone back to their brothers,

00:12:31.810 --> 00:12:36.690
then the only place they can return to has got to be Kamogawa!

00:12:38.570 --> 00:12:41.780
Are you going to just let her go?

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:43.990
There are no more operating shuttles to take her back to shore.

00:12:43.990 --> 00:12:46.700
There's no way she can leave Pharos.

00:12:58.630 --> 00:13:00.960
Lan... Muginami...

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:06.050
She hasn't changed at all, that Madoka.

00:13:06.890 --> 00:13:12.970
Lord Villagiulio, over half a day has passed since we lost Muginami's signal.

00:13:12.970 --> 00:13:17.100
Even if she is on the run from the Le Garite force, isn't that a bit too long?

00:13:19.150 --> 00:13:23.440
You allowed her to act on her own under the assumption that if Aura fell into Le Garite's hands,

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:27.700
Muginami would personally deal with Kyouno Madoka, right?

00:13:28.530 --> 00:13:31.120
But if she is having second thoughts,

00:13:31.120 --> 00:13:32.540
then maybe you should order her to—

00:13:32.540 --> 00:13:34.040
I will not give the order.

00:13:34.540 --> 00:13:35.910
Haven't I already said so before?

00:13:35.910 --> 00:13:37.540
I won't do what Dizel would do.

00:13:37.540 --> 00:13:38.460
But...

00:13:38.790 --> 00:13:43.130
He plans to sacrifice our planet for his to survive.

00:13:43.130 --> 00:13:44.880
Thus I must oppose him.

00:13:44.880 --> 00:13:48.970
Who am I to tell Muginami to bury her feelings?

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:53.470
If I did, I'd be betraying the very ideal for which I took the throne.

00:13:55.350 --> 00:13:57.600
She'll show up in time,

00:13:58.390 --> 00:14:01.900
along with whatever result her feelings have wrought.

